 are responsible for processing requests, applying)Tj T* (business logic, working with databases, authentication and generating responses. Examples include Node.js, PHP,)Tj T* (Python/Django and Java/Spring.)Tj T* T*/F2 9.5 Tf (Major Differences:)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf T* <7f20>Tj/F2 9.5 Tf (Execution:)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( Client-side runs in the browser; server-side runs on the server.)Tj T* <7f20>Tj/F2 9.5 Tf (Main purpose:)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( Client-side handles presentation and user interaction; server-side handles processing and data)Tj T* (management.)Tj T* <7f20>Tj/F2 9.5 Tf (Examples:)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( HTML/CSS/JavaScript are client-side technologies; Node.js/PHP/Python are common server-side)Tj T* (technologies.)Tj T* <7f20>Tj/F2 9.5 Tf (Database:)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( Server-side applications commonly communicate with databases, while client-side code normally)Tj T* (receives data through server APIs.)Tj T* T* (Therefore, both sides work together: the client provides the user interface, while the server provides processing and)Tj T* (data services.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54.18898 167.3701 cm .752941 0 0 rg BT 15 TL/F3 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (Q4. Block-Level Elements in HTML)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54.18898 143.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F3 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (Ans.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54.18898 53.37008 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 74.5 Tm (Block-level elements are HTML elements that normally start from a new line and take up the available horizontal)Tj T* (space of their containing element. They are mainly used to organize content into separate sections or blocks.)Tj T* T*/F2 9.5 Tf (Characteristics:)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf T* (1. They normally begin on a new line.)Tj T* (2. They generally occupy the available width of their parent container.)Tj T* ET Q Q
